{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog","id":430490,"title":"Invictus Merits and Oaths: The Ties That Bind [Secrets of the Covenants dev blog]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-06T12:23:50-08:00","id":430490,"title":"Invictus Merits and Oaths: The Ties That Bind [Secrets of the Covenants dev blog]","content":"<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1B3dwo3Dzg1h3BKf2gb7Am3NTS01Bu87lKPV46AtUySg/mobilebasic?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...ilebasic?pli=1</a><br /> <br /> So, ladies and gents, what do we think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 03-09-2015, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T12:27:27-08:00","id":430509,"title":"","content":"Aww, Courtoisie is a Fighting Style any Invictus can buy? What does that mean for my beloved Spina?<br /> <br /> EDIT: also, &quot;Invested&quot; is already the name of an Inictus-only Merit in VtR 2e, so the one in here is going to need a new name,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-06-2015, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T12:41:14-08:00","id":430515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=430509#post430509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aww, Courtoisie is a Fighting Style any Invictus can buy? What does that mean for my beloved Spina?</div> </div> </div> </div>Free dots? A superior version? A Gift that synergizes with the merit?<br /> <br /> I like a lot of these Merits, and it's nice to see some Oaths that help define the internal interactions of the Invictus. Oaths make a lot of sense as a means of facilitating business between a bunch of people that don't always trust one another/might compete for the same resources.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I really dig stuff like Prestigious Sire or Social Engineering, though I feel the prerequisite is a lot in the case of Prestigious Sire, when it's so similar to the first dot of Dynasty Membership.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 03-06-2015, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T13:39:42-08:00","id":430542,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Oath of Abstinence ... wow.<br /> <br /> I wonder if the oathsworn person still hungers for the blood?</span></b></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T13:56:19-08:00","id":430569,"title":"","content":"So, general opinions, can Invictus believably hold its own against the Carthians with this muscle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T14:10:04-08:00","id":430593,"title":"","content":"Probably. I mean, it's not like it stops them from frenzying, and what happens when their vitae pool gets them into the Hungry and Starving ranges?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T14:26:07-08:00","id":430608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=430569#post430569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, general opinions, can Invictus believably hold its own against the Carthians with this muscle?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not currently. All the decent merits can be obtained by anyone with a single point of covenant status. The Carthians can also steal them for themself or strip away the prerequisite Invictus covenant status from another character to nullify them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=430593#post430593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> what happens when their vitae pool gets them into the Hungry and Starving ranges?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why they pledge fealty to someone for the mystic vitae transfer. Or they simply feed when they are hungry, spend the vitae to swear the oath again, and fill up on Vitae before they spend the last willpower to activate the oath again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T14:28:02-08:00","id":430615,"title":"","content":"It seems to me some of these Oaths could benefit from a mutual end without penalties clause. Social Engineering could be problematic, 10 minutes to find and stake a vampire in their home without penalty. Does Haven still work during this time? At least that allows the vampire a good chance to wake up. I think I'll add it won't work when seeking to commit violence in the Safe Place.<br /> <br /> Glad to see open development continue. I was starting to wonder about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 03-06-2015, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T14:35:29-08:00","id":430622,"title":"","content":"They can wreck Carthians with the help of Social Engineering to nix all of their Carthian bennies. I wonder if Trained Observer applies to that.<br /> <br /> I do kind of like the technology angle. It feels more... &quot;right&quot; for it to be in the hands of the ivory tower. I do notice a lot of things don't actually require Invictus Status, though (like Tech Savvy). Is this intentional?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T14:45:26-08:00","id":430628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=430622#post430622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can wreck Carthians with the help of Social Engineering to nix all of their Carthian bennies. I wonder if Trained Observer applies to that.<br /> <br /> I do kind of like the technology angle. It feels more... &quot;right&quot; for it to be in the hands of the ivory tower. I do notice a lot of things don't actually require Invictus Status, though (like Tech Savvy). Is this intentional?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think so, like the merits in the Carthian playtest, not all of them seem like things the Invictus would exclusively do, just things that they would typically do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T14:47:54-08:00","id":430632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=430569#post430569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, general opinions, can Invictus believably hold its own against the Carthians with this muscle?</div> </div> </div> </div>More or less. The Carthians have some big guns, but those are harder to use in comparison to the multitude of weapons the Invictus have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T15:01:49-08:00","id":430640,"title":"","content":"Question, is Crowdsourcing meant to be explicitly Invictus? It seems like it would, reflecting the unique way that the Covenant pools resources, as opposed to the general sharing that Carthians seem to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T15:17:17-08:00","id":430645,"title":"","content":"According to the playtest doc: &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Members of the Invictus have access to the following Merits. Unless otherwise noted, they have an additional prerequisite of Status (Invictus) \u2022 or higher.&quot;</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T15:18:24-08:00","id":430648,"title":"","content":"It does say this at the start.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;Members of the Invictus have access to the following Merits. Unless otherwise noted, they have an additional prerequisite of Status (Invictus) \u2022 or higher&quot;<br /> <br /> So that answers the question of if you can take them without being Invictus.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2989-violetdea","name":"violetdea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T15:33:56-08:00","id":430707,"title":"","content":"Oath of the True Knight, you say?<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/STXL1Hy.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I am looking forward to fiction involving InBoard.<br /> <br /> On the note of Oaths, given how increasingly arcane these Oaths seem to be getting, I would love to have some possible in-setting explanations where they and Carthian Law come from. I seem to recall the devs mentioned they would put some possible ideas for Carthian Law into the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T16:45:35-08:00","id":430804,"title":"","content":"These new Oaths...<br /> <br /> Oath of the Refugee is <i>an</i> excellent way to get out of Dodge.<br /> <br /> But Oath of the Model Prisoner is <i>awesome</i>. Other than that, you kinda want Invictus in charge because Oath of Office and Noblesse Oblige give them a <i>big</i> incentive to be non-corrupt officials. I mean, the only way that could be more perfect is if Noblesse Oblige would allow other people to talk you out of Frenzy as if they were a Touchstone, but only if they bring up your job, and how your Frenzy is impacting it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T16:58:50-08:00","id":430836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=430804#post430804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, the only way that could be more perfect is if Noblesse Oblige would allow other people to talk you out of Frenzy as if they were a Touchstone, but only if they bring up your job, and how your Frenzy is impacting it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Y'know, who says that is not the case?<br /> <br /> Good ideas are good ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T16:59:53-08:00","id":430838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=430707#post430707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oath of the True Knight, you say?<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/STXL1Hy.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I am looking forward to fiction involving InBoard.<br /> <br /> On the note of Oaths, given how increasingly arcane these Oaths seem to be getting, I would love to have some possible in-setting explanations where they and Carthian Law come from. I seem to recall the devs mentioned they would put some possible ideas for Carthian Law into the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's see how second drafts go. But I put some super oblique references to what Carthian Law might be into the Carthian chapter. I didn't want to be too definitive though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T17:04:35-08:00","id":430848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=430838#post430838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's see how second drafts go. But I put some super oblique references to what Carthian Law might be into the Carthian chapter. I didn't want to be too definitive though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I totally get that and agree. I am just wondering about whether we can get a grab bag of potential ideas. Some Carthian philosophers and thinkers must have had some clever thoughts about it at some point.<br /> <br /> May I also ask a related crossover question (to which you may or may not be able to give an official answer)? Can other supernaturals attuned to Fate or sympathetic connections possibly see the connections between Oathed Kindred?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T17:25:36-08:00","id":430864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=430848#post430848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I totally get that and agree. I am just wondering about whether we can get a grab bag of potential ideas. Some Carthian philosophers and thinkers must have had some clever thoughts about it at some point.<br /> <br /> May I also ask a related crossover question (to which you may or may not be able to give an official answer)? Can other supernaturals attuned to Fate or sympathetic connections possibly see the connections between Oathed Kindred?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would allow it. The relationship is palpable and definite, so sure. And it seeds all sorts of fun plot questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T00:59:36-08:00","id":431134,"title":"","content":"It appears some of the new oaths are of a different kind then the ones introduced in the core rulebook. The Oath of Abstinence, Oath of the Refugee and The Oath of the True Knight do not appear to have a liege and a vassal, but are a kind of personal vow (not sure about the Oaths of Office and Hard Motherfucker). I assume those oaths are the ones which are &quot;available to Invictus characters that meet the prerequisites&quot; as mentioned in the header. I also assume they still must be sworn before a notary.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1281-aegontargaryen","name":"AegonTargaryen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1281_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T11:38:23-08:00","id":431577,"title":"","content":"<b>Abstinence</b> - If there wasn't such a potentially high vitae cost, I could see using this as a temporary measure in a few situations. Living on someone's hunting grounds for a time without putting pressure on the herd - a further way to actually handle long-term imprisonment (<i>You can keep me locked in this room for eternity, Prince</i>). Also - knight-guardians at their same posts throughout the years just waiting for an enemy to come. Clarification on what &quot;imbibe&quot; means could help - see if you *can* stack this with mystical blood transfers of other Oaths, etc.<br /> <br /> <b>Handshake Deal</b> - Awesome.<br /> <br /> <b>Hard Motherfucker</b> - Not sure how I feel about this one. I like the deliberate conflict it causes between Inv/Car - but I wonder if the trade off should be a little worse. You're losing experiences, but maybe there should be some additional pressure to end a traitor. Or a traitor, once revenged upon, is freed/forgiven so as to not see a chain of new recruits kicking the shit out of the same guy but always letting them go. Probably just addressed by the table, though. I suspect there should also be a Sanctity of Merits comment for non-betrayal changes. Someone who's promoted up from the coterie would get to respend those Merit Dots, or redefine their role as a higher status Invictus member, rather than a coterie member.<br /> <br /> <b>Model Prisoner</b> - Really like this one. &quot;<i>Oh - I'll surrender peacefully, but the Prince will know exactly how I'm treated.</i>&quot; A little put off by the mystical damage bit, would almost rather the damage was Government Merit suppression instead. Like - the officer who ignores the mistreated prisoner loses City/Cov Status unless they punish the offenders or free the prisoner, etc, or maybe even becomes a Masquerade threat themselves because of the wounds (some sort of social penalties rather than wound penalties).<br /> <br /> <b>Office</b> - Love it. I would totally agree that a meaningful service to their officer duties counts exactly like a meaningful interaction with a Touchstone, including frenzy talkdown attempts. <br /> <br /> <b>Refugee</b> - Interesting, and a good balance to the Carthian 'city invasion' Merits.<br /> <br /> <b>Righteous Kill</b> - I like the idea of ritualized pre-remorse for a sin a lot, though I could also see this being a specialized Sanctified-Invictus oath crossover rather than a purely specific Invictus Oath. And it looks like the best 'confessor' is a low humanity Kindred. For many sins they won't even need to test at all, nevermind the bonus die. I hope there a bit of specificity involved: &quot;Sire, I need to kill <i>these three</i> individuals, they are the ones who witnessed the Primogen's frenzy.&quot; - And those specific killings are affected, rather than a blanket &quot;I made the Oath, now I can kill anyone related to the case as long as I can justify it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Safe Word</b> - The other one I'm not sure on without some play examples. Feel like there could be some other interesting asymmetry without it being a primarily combat trump. I suppose you could use it just as someone was giving a speech before the court or the like, but most often I suspect it will be used as part of a combat roll.<br /> <br /> <b>True Knight</b> - Like it a lot. Curious if there will be different interpretations regarding &quot;neutrality&quot; between the differences of Knightly Orders. Also, can you violate this Oath, and if so presumably Sanctity of Merits would <i>not</i> apply?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T16:19:48-08:00","id":431961,"title":"","content":"I think the point between <b>Safe Word</b> is that it's a way to get someone to trust you. It's giving someone power over you as a sign of goodwill.<br /> <br /> It also makes coteries of Invictus <i>terrifying</i>; imagine, if you would, a group of, say, five Invictus who have sworn the Oath of the Safe Word to each-other. You have a group of five Vampires who <i>pool their Willpower pools</i>, and who each have the best social merit of each member.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, imagine an Invictus sworn into the office of Sheriff who has an Oath of Office sworn for their position and an Oath of the Safe Word running with the Prince, who 'shares' their City Status \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 with the Sheriff. That Sheriff has a <i>big</i> Willpower pool, and gets +5 dice when spending Willpower.<br /> <br /> Combine that with swearing an Oath of the True Knight, and you've got an almost ideal enforcer.<br /> <br /> Ooh, and Oath of the Handshake Deal can be used by Invictus rulers to help police criminals; the criminal has to make an oath to not commit a crime, the Invictus makes a token oath, and they shake on it. If the criminal commits a crime, the city immediately and permanently claims their wealth or their allies or their True Friend or whatever.<br /> <br /> Now I'm stuck trying to think of how hardcore crazy a joint exercise of Law and Oath would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T18:23:30-08:00","id":432089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=431961#post431961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm stuck trying to think of how hardcore crazy a joint exercise of Law and Oath would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've had it in my most recent chronicle. It was scary. That is an understatement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member