caneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T19:19:41-08:00","id":432136,"title":"","content":"I have a question: does Oath of the True Knight prevent you from having oaths like Oath of the Handshake Deal and Oath of the Safe Word?<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> I wonder if it would be more in-line with the fluff if the Oath just prevented you from being the Vassal of an Oath?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T19:45:49-08:00","id":432149,"title":"","content":"So after that terrifying picture was painted, I have to ask what happens when you add a Strix into the mix? Is an Oath broken when a vampire takes an Oath then becomes possessed by a Strix then commits acts against the Oath?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T04:39:48-07:00","id":432452,"title":"","content":"Can't people just prevent you from using oath of the model prisoner? You need a notary to activate an oath. They can just keep you from one if they want to mistreat you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2572-hugsworth","name":"Hugsworth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T05:04:54-07:00","id":432521,"title":"","content":"Some of those merits shouldn't require invictus membership, really: Prestigious Sire, Social Engineering, and Tech Savvy, while undoubtedly more common among invictus nothing about them says invictus only to me. <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Courtoisie might be a secret, I could see that.<br /> <br /> Oath of Abstinance- I like it, but seems rather annoying to me that it's something you'd need to do over and over again, since even without expending blood to wake up you're going to run out of blood thanks to discipline use or healing. <br /> </span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T06:32:55-07:00","id":432577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hugsworth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=432452#post432452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't people just prevent you from using oath of the model prisoner? You need a notary to activate an oath. They can just keep you from one if they want to mistreat you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Be your own notary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T06:51:56-07:00","id":432585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=432149#post432149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So after that terrifying picture was painted, I have to ask what happens when you add a Strix into the mix? Is an Oath broken when a vampire takes an Oath then becomes possessed by a Strix then commits acts against the Oath?</div> </div> </div> </div>Possessing Strix cannot benefit from Oaths and the other party loses the benefit as well. Which is a really handy Strix-identifier, BTW...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T12:26:41-07:00","id":432936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=432585#post432585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Possessing Strix cannot benefit from Oaths and the other party loses the benefit as well. Which is a really handy Strix-identifier, BTW...</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm...<br /> <br /> I'm trying to think of an Oath that you could <i>use</i> as a way to consistently check this in-game. They either have subtle effects or would be overly onerous to try to break all the time (and that would get you into Invictus trouble. Staking-and-left-for-the-sun trouble).<br /> <br /> I mean, a group of Invictus swearing the Oath of the Safe Word <i>might</i> work if the ST feels that you can &quot;feel&quot; the extra reserves of will IC. Just swear it in a ring, like so:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> A\u2192B\u2192C\u2192D\u2192E\u2192A.</div> <br /> If, say, B became possessed by a Strix, A and C become aware that one part of their extra reserves of will was just removed. They just need to contact everyone else in the ring, and logical deduction tells you who was Strix'd. It'd be better if there was some Oath that allowed you to mentally contact your Liege/Vassal (through Blood Sympathy) with a short message; use that to &quot;check-in&quot; with everyone each night, and anyone who doesn't respond within a set time frame is under suspicion for being a Strix. If a majority of Kindred don't get a response, stake and bake 'em.<br /> <br /> Of course, all of this is pretty fallible, and relies on Vampires <i>trusting</i> each-other. Which is... unlikely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T14:40:39-07:00","id":433136,"title":"","content":"I forgot about that. A character is only allowed to be a part of one Safe Word Oath so that won't work. Handshake Deal not to get possessed? Simple Fealty Oath with the protocol of telling a lie when beginning a conversation might work. Of course, it would only work for the liege when identifying Strix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T15:16:37-07:00","id":433191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=433136#post433136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forgot about that. A character is only allowed to be a part of one Safe Word Oath so that won't work. Handshake Deal not to get possessed? Simple Fealty Oath with the protocol of telling a lie when beginning a conversation might work. Of course, it would only work for the liege when identifying Strix.</div> </div> </div> </div>I keep missing the one-per-oath thing on Oath of the Safe Word. Oh well.<br /> <br /> Though that might make an interesting Oath; empower an office to let it act as a &quot;person&quot;. So you can swear an Oath as John Q. Bloodsucker, and another as Secretary of Internal Security. As long as you're in that Office, those Oaths apply to you... but those Oaths are made by <i>the Office</i>, not you. So if &quot;The Secretary of Internal Security&quot; swears a Fealty Oath to the Prince, John Q. Bloodsucker benefits from the Fealty Oath as well; however, if he gets staked or otherwise replaced by Susie Q. Leech, then the benefits of that Oath transfer to Susie.<br /> <br /> Not sure what drawback that Oath should have; maybe you only benefit while on official business? So if someone defaults their personal fortune to the Secretary of Internal Security (they break a Handshake Deal with a collateral of Resources \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022), John or Susie could use those resources while on official business, but not to buy personal friends a present or to fund a personal project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T04:44:11-07:00","id":433795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=432577#post432577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Be your own notary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, some of those really feel like they should not need the Notary to involve themselves... perhaps some can be exempt from requiring a Notary? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T05:00:32-07:00","id":433799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=433795#post433795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, some of those really feel like they should not need the Notary to involve themselves... perhaps some can be exempt from requiring a Notary? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. These new oaths are a lot different. All the old ones involved a vassal and a liege. These new ones seem more like you're signing a contract with a changeling or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2572-hugsworth","name":"Hugsworth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T05:06:13-07:00","id":433804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hugsworth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=433799#post433799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. These new oaths are a lot different. All the old ones involved a vassal and a liege. These new ones seem more like you're signing a contract with a changeling or something.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Some of them also feel a bit overly specific in my opinion (not the Oaths, but the merits)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T06:41:07-07:00","id":433889,"title":"","content":"Crowdsourcing seems quite cool, but there's not (to my knowledge) been any guidance on what more than 5 dots of Resources (for example) would actually involve. At what dot rating can I initiate a takeover of a major company? Or is 8 dots of Resources private country money? I'd really like to see some guidelines on this.<br /> <br /> Also the downside of Crowdsourcing is unclear: &quot;Then, those Merits are lost. The original owner loses access to them for the remainder of the story.&quot;<br /> <br /> Does that mean that the dot contributed is lost for the remainder of the story, or the <b>Merit</b> is lost? The idea of contributing a dot from my five to a crowdsourcing project only to see my entire wealth inaccessible for an extended period is totally unappealing, so I guess it must be the former - it might be worth explicitly saying that.<br /> <br /> Information Network is a really cool idea, but I don't think it's taken far enough. In fact, that's a criticism I'd level at a number of these merits (Moderator, Social Engineering and Tech Savvy all especially jump out).<br /> <br /> I think it might be better to reconstitute these merits as Styles of a kind, interplaying with the social manoeuvring (doors) mechanics and changing how other merits work (especially the workhorse Resources, Contacts and Allies) rather than just giving specific bonuses in specific scenarios. I'd love to see something more like (just hashed together quickly, obviously):<br /> <b>Network(\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Style)</b><br /><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Manipulation \u2022\u2022\u2022, Wits \u2022\u2022\u2022. You must also possess the Contacts merit at least equal to the dot rating of this style you wish to buy.<br /> The Invictus capitalise on their associates more comprehensively and brutally than other covenants can manage, turning their casual contacts and sources of information into a fully fledged spy network as their control over their associates increases.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Network can only be used with Contacts you have an established connection with (i.e. possess the merit pertaining to). Casual contacts and associates cannot be leveraged using this style. Your character gains access to the following abilities at each level:<br /> <b>Information Network (\u2022):</b> Every Contact your character counts as a Skill Specialty related to the information he provides. However, she may only use that Specialty when utilizing information gained from the Contact. If she loses the Contact for whatever reason, she also loses the Specialty.<br /> <b>Corroborating Evidence (\u2022\u2022): </b>Your character can use multiple contacts to get better information than would otherwise be available by combining their reports into a comprehensive source. When you roll to access information from a Contact and have a second Contact that might be able to provide additional information about that subject, however tangential, and succeed you also immediately get the Informed condition pertaining to the information you gathered.<br /> <b>Vicious Rumours (\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>You can now use Contacts to dig up blackmail material about your enemies - worse, you can use the information gathered to viciously invent plausible rumours that they are going to have trouble disproving. A valid use of a contact is now to create the Leveraged condition on a target, even if they do not have anything obvious to be Leveraged. The storyteller can rule this is inappropriate in some situations, but should be lenient with its application.<br /> <b>Sword of Damocles (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>Many kindred have contacts, but few possess the kind of damning knowledge that you can glean from yours. If you are interacting with someone who possess the Leveraged condition (and they don't resolve it) created by Vicious Rumours or about whom you have the Informed condition from Corroborating Evidence, you are also considered to have hard leverage substantial enough to remove two doors when forcing them as part of a social maneuver. <br /> <b>Spin the Web (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>Your character has gone beyond simply gathering information from his sources - now she can create it whole cloth. You can access your contacts to, instead of discovering information, provide it to them. Such information spreads like wildfire within their organisation and is seem to have come from a trusted source. This can quickly destabilise organisations, cause chaos on the markets, or disrupt whole cities if used carefully. The rumours die down after a while, or after definitive proof is produced that shows it as a lie, so the canny kindred uses it to spread vicious truth rather than lies if possible, and always times the introduction of such information carefully. Mechanically, anyone who is affected by the rumour is considered to have one less door when the character is trying to convince them of something related to it, but the narrative effects can go much further.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/33-nifara","name":"Nifara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar33_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T14:51:49-07:00","id":434609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hugsworth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=432452#post432452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't people just prevent you from using oath of the model prisoner? You need a notary to activate an oath. They can just keep you from one if they want to mistreat you.</div> </div> </div> </div>They probably could but then you might try to escape so they would need to assign guards to watch over you. Which could be a real hassle if you're there for a long time (and in the case of a vampire, long time is a looong time). With the oath all they need to do is give you some blood once a day. Two-sided coin I guess <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/640-bram_pc","name":"Bram_pc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar640_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T15:27:19-07:00","id":434701,"title":"","content":"&lt;&lt; Crowdsourcing seems quite cool, but there's not (to my knowledge) been any guidance on what more than 5 dots of Resources (for example) would actually involve. At what dot rating can I initiate a takeover of a major company? Or is 8 dots of Resources private country money? I'd really like to see some guidelines on this.&gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> Requiem Chronicler's Guide and Damnation City both have rules on handling Resources above 5.<br /> <br /> &lt;&lt; Also the downside of Crowdsourcing is unclear: &quot;Then, those Merits are lost. The original owner loses access to them for the remainder of the story. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> The phrasing isn't the best, but I'm assuming it means whoever is the beneficiary of the merit transfer for purposes of whatever action is being undertaken requiring them to be pooled together gets them for whatever action, then they lose them. They don't get to continue strutting around town with an effective 15 Resources 13 Contacts or whatever for the rest of the story. Whoever loaned X dots of merits does not have them for the rest of the story. It's basically the same mechanics used for purchasing something using Resources extended to other merits.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T11:35:27-07:00","id":436005,"title":"","content":"*reads Courtoisie*<br /> <br /> ... Is it bad that I want to play a Vampire Guybrush Threepwood now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T14:37:28-07:00","id":436277,"title":"","content":"I was thinking more this way. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kRAI9_MkmBM\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kRAI9_MkmBM</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T14:43:31-07:00","id":436284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andreamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=436005#post436005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*reads Courtoisie*<br /> <br /> ... Is it bad that I want to play a Vampire Guybrush Threepwood now?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is, in fact, the correct response.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T19:26:54-07:00","id":436550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andreamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=436005#post436005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*reads Courtoisie*<br /> <br /> ... Is it bad that I want to play a Vampire Guybrush Threepwood now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good catch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T00:31:49-07:00","id":436803,"title":"","content":"So is Courtoisie supposed to be one of those rare few examples of things which allows you to deal lethal damage to Kindred with weapons? I only ask because it says lethal damage, but doesn't mention the targets in question. I know thematically it's supposed to be like more of a Vamp on Vamp duel thing, but just wanted to be sure!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T01:41:21-07:00","id":436826,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nifara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=433889#post433889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Information Network is a really cool idea, but I don't think it's taken far enough. In fact, that's a criticism I'd level at a number of these merits (Moderator, Social Engineering and Tech Savvy all especially jump out).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with you on Moderator and Information Network.<br /> <br /> Here's the troublesome spot for me on Moderator:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moderator Merit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Once per <b>story</b>, she can use <b>a dot</b> in this Merit as a dot in Allies, Contacts, or Library. The utilized Merit cannot be local, and is limited by its Internet-based access.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\">Emphasis mine. The syntax reads that it's actually pointless to have more than one dot in the Merit, as you can only use it once per story.<br /> <br /> As for Information Network, I'm not sure why you'd purchase the Merit when you could purchase the relevant Specialty as they're the same price anyway.</span></span><br /> <br /> As for the Oaths, I'm a bit confused as to how the apply with the Notary Merit in VtR 2e. Previously I believe you had to possess the Notary Merit to seal Oaths, but a lot of these can be taught to outsiders and the like. Maybe a Notary must teach at least one of the relevant parties the Oath?<br /> <br /> Otherwise I'm pretty keen on these, particularly the Merit for non-Invictus.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T10:49:38-07:00","id":437225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=436826#post436826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><br /> I'm with you on Moderator and Information Network.<br /> <br /> Here's the troublesome spot for me on Moderator:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Emphasis mine. The syntax reads that it's actually pointless to have more than one dot in the Merit, as you can only use it once per story.<br /> <br /> As for Information Network, I'm not sure why you'd purchase the Merit when you could purchase the relevant Specialty as they're the same price anyway.</span></span><br /> <br /> As for the Oaths, I'm a bit confused as to how the apply with the Notary Merit in VtR 2e. Previously I believe you had to possess the Notary Merit to seal Oaths, but a lot of these can be taught to outsiders and the like. Maybe a Notary must teach at least one of the relevant parties the Oath?<br /> <br /> Otherwise I'm pretty keen on these, particularly the Merit for non-Invictus.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>You just need to swear them <i>in front of</i> a Notary. Basically, if you don't have a Notary available, the Oath doesn't &quot;stick&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T11:14:38-07:00","id":437271,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Notaries are sort of like the witness who actually knows how to make the magic work, while the people involved in the Oath are basically like &quot;hey mr. notary this is what we wanna do please help&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T11:58:09-07:00","id":437304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichE</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=436803#post436803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is Courtoisie supposed to be one of those rare few examples of things which allows you to deal lethal damage to Kindred with weapons? I only ask because it says lethal damage, but doesn't mention the targets in question. I know thematically it's supposed to be like more of a Vamp on Vamp duel thing, but just wanted to be sure!</div> </div> </div> </div>There is nothing that indicates this style allows weapons to deal lethal damage to kindred. It will deal lethal damage if it is used in conjunction with kindred dueling merit from the vampire core book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T12:29:48-07:00","id":437350,"title":"","content":"Mmm... not sure I enjoy the Cortoisie Fighting Style.<br /> <br /> There is absolutely no reason why any Invictus wouldn't get it. They are bound to have one of those Abilities at a high level, and for 2 points they can use them in combat when it arises.<br /> <br /> In contrast the Circle of the Crone one isn't very useful to non-combatants in the least, but very useful to temple defenders.<br /> <br /> <br /> Additionally, it feels pretty supernatural, but I guess that is a new theme of things.<br /> <br /> <br /> One last worry, though... where does this leave the Spina? Are they gone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>IA","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/462-tchokes","name":"Tchokes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T14:38:06-07:00","id":437547,"title":"","content":"I am sorry but I have to disagree. Firstly, it has a prerequisite of Weaponry 2 and not every Unconquered will prefer the use of melee weaponry over guns or fists. Secondly, except for the second dot, it actually does not help in overcoming a superior foe, unlike most Fighting Styles, and even the second dot is limited since you can only (at least by the current wording) exchange either a Skill or an Attribute, not both, so you still need a good physical Skill or Attribute to pair with.<br /> <br /> In fact, if I would level a criticism against it, is that for a supposed duelling fighting style it actually does not help all that much in a proper duel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T16:57:46-07:00","id":437715,"title":"","content":"My impression was they cheat. I don't think they go for &quot;proper duels.&quot; I can see them going for the appearance of a proper duel. I guess they don't call themselves Unconquered for nothing. If you ain't cheating, you ain't trying. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T06:56:29-07:00","id":441253,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think these are terrible. How exactly is Invictus uniquely positioned to prevent the Acolytes from summoning Cthulu and turning the place into Hell on Earth or ensuring kindred society is not overthrown by a Dragon with a god-complex, a few scales and coils, and a couple of ideas on how to make the local kindred more useful to stroking his ego, or even keeping the Sanctified from marching out on a genocidal purge? Acolytes get to construct frankenstein monsters or summon monsters, Dragons get loads of additional psychic powers otherwise closed to vampires and resistances to disciplines, and Carthians (just like Sanctified and Acolyte spellcasters) can mystically deliver unavoidable and unresistable crippling strikes or death blows but the best thing you come up with for Invictus is the ability to skip eating for a few nights if they already have lots of willpower and vitae to blow already.<br /> <br /> I don't care for the oath system because much of it literally rewards oathbreakers and punishes individuals who act in good faith. This is only intensified when you flushed the few restrictions that were the only pretense anyone could claim Oaths are an Invictus signatory ability, as well as the only real deterrence against abuse, down the toilet.<br /> <br /> Oath of Abstinence<br /> Because Elders (Invictus and otherwise) don't already have multiple methods of circumventing the vinculum dangers attendant with consuming kindred blood. But don't even think of using your disciplines.<br /> <br /> Oath of the Hard Motherfucker<br /> That's a name I expect the Carthians to use in reference to this oath especially due to it's purpose. Why doesn't the Invictus use a name for it that sounds a tad bit more professional and not the ghetto fabulous pejorative currently being used?<br /> <br /> Oath of the Safe Word<br /> This strikes me as something that would be used as a punitive judgement for a minor offense.<br /> <br /> Oath of the Handshake Deal<br /> Can covenant status be offered as collateral? Because if so, this is the &quot;I steal ur powrz&quot; power like everyone else has gotten.<br /> <br /> Oath of the Refugee<br /> You have status equal to zero when you flee a city so you cancel out zero successes to any efforts to pursue or attack you. Also, why wouldn't the Sanctity of Merits apply when you lost the attendant city and covenant status?<br /> <br /> Oath of the Model Prisoner<br /> This one makes no sense to me. In my experience kindred taken prisoner (and if it's known they are kindred) are kept staked when they aren't being actively questioned or needed conscious for an experiment until or unless they are released. It's easier to hide or transport them when you can stuff them in a duffel bag or throw them in a shallow grave or freezer and not actually worry about killing them permanently. Keeping them in torpor also means (most of the time) the captive can't spend idle time plotting to use Protean, Obfuscate, Dominate, Majesty, Animalism, Nightmare etc. to overpower their captors and flee. Since this oath explicitly doesn't require a notary and does direct Aggravated or Lethal damage it has the greatest potential for abuse. But we'll pretend for a moment that vampires are not pragmatic and that they follow the Geneva Conventions. Creative applications can have this oath apply to being kidnapped or otherwise 'unjustly' detained. Even overthrow a prince. Captors can get around the restrictions by subcontracting interrogation or imprisonment to individuals or groups who are not covenant members.<br /> <br /> Oath of the True Knight<br /> Does this oath require you to end previously existing oaths and vinculums and forswear other covenant and city (and possibly clan) affiliations first, or does it dissolve them when the oath is taken. Everyone else so far has gotten the ability to become immune to vinculums or break the blood bond prematurely, so I see no particular reason why it wouldn't dissolve pre-existing obligations. But it's unclear on that point as well as whether or not its the knight or the one attempting to force a vinculum as the one who takes Aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> Invested<br /> As has been stated previously, another merit already exists with the same name. This is a cut and paste of the same merit every other covenant has gotten to give PCs a jump on status accumulation into a covenant they don't currently belong to formally.<br /> I don't like these merits because if you have a non-hostile relationship with someone in a given covenant you should already be able to trade minor favors in the form of a single dot of a social merit already. If you're referring to the limited access to their covenant signature abilities like Coils and Cruac, well, Invictus doesn't have any signature abilities to share and they don't have any useful merits requiring more than one covenant status to obtain, so why bother?<br /> <br /> Courtoisie<br /> Considering some of the comments in this thread, it's obvious that it's not being taken seriously as a fighting style. Then again, not only does it use the same name as the bloodline signature discipline of the foppish Spina bloodline, it's a subpar fighting style currently. While the other covenants actually has abilities to improve their survivability or lethal ability in combat, the Invictus opts to becomes Spider-man, trading quips during a fight for actual lethality. The only really useful ability is Establish the Duel and that's only IF it works automatically even if another character is attempting to sneak up on you to stab you in the back using Obfuscate and breaks the discipline's effects. It's not even particularly useful against multiple attackers because switching to the more dangerous foe or not persisting in beating on someone who's fleeing, torpid, or dead, ends the benefit.<br /> <br /> Crowdsourcing<br /> This looks like a variant of Carthian Pull and Attache applied to PCs instead of a Retainer. This is sort of something I could see a Commissioner in Invictus having but since they officially don't have any titles beyond Notary, and that was rendered obsolete with the proposal regarding oaths here. Why should anyone bother with more than one dot? Why do you need Academics, it has nothing to do with gaining or applying a formal education? Unless Carthian Pull is hard capped at 5, it's superior to Crowdsourcing.<br /> <br /> Moderator<br /> Another one where nobody should actually bother with more than one dot. Someone with 3 ranks in Computers should already be able to use the Internet as a 1 dot Library, Allies, or Contacts with limited value and functionality.<br /> <br /> Information Network<br /> Unless the specialty is interdisciplinary or considered an area of expertise, this merit isn't worth purchasing.<br /> <br /> Prestigious Sire<br /> Another merit mash up. Mentor with rank 1 of Dynasty Membership. A 4 dot Mentor can already use his (presumably) superior social skills and status to speak on your behalf. If your social interaction ability is so questionable, you're better off investing in that as well as Dynasty Membership and a rank or two in Etiquette rather than this merit that only lets you situationally leech off another character's status ratings.<br /> <br /> Tech Savvy<br /> While there is an actual mechanical purpose to the tiers here, it's unnecessary. You can't jury rig something together that's functional with all those prerequisites already? And since when could you no longer obtain equipment with improved Durability, functionality etc. than the default versions if you had the Resources score? Is this merit supposed to enable Invictus members to obtain equipment type Hunter Endowments?<br /> <br /> Noblesse Oblige<br /> This merit may not be advisable for someone who is upwardly mobile since they would likely lose their official position for another one if they got promoted. But I can also see it as a mechanic who's purpose is to actually kill any desire for upward mobility.<br /> <br /> Social Engineering<br /> Interesting idea, kind of lackluster in some of the effects for a four dot merit with some extensive prerequisites. There are no examples for using social engineering to prop someone up (in other words, moving a mortal associate up within an organization to where he's a more useful retainer or ally, or even a kindred protege.)<br /> <br /> <i>A +1 bonus to a Social roll against the victim, or -1 on one of their Social rolls. Another character can access the bonus or take advantage of the penalty if the information is shared.</i><br /> <br /> A mere +1 bonus to a single Social roll against the target? I can get more using the Willpower point straightforward to apply to that roll.<br /> <br /> <i>A damning piece of information that, when used, removes a dot from the character\u2019s Allies, Contacts, Feeding Grounds, Herd, or Status. The Merit is eligible for Sanctity of Merits.</i><br /> <br /> If they're capable if instantly buying the lost dot back with a convincing display of crocodile tears or application of a discipline (that probably helped them get said merit in the first place.) why bother? Even blowing a Prestigious Sire roll has restrictions on when you can buy it back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","user":"Audrey St. John","date":". 03-14-2015, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T09:27:21-07:00","id":441445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=431961#post431961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm stuck trying to think of how hardcore crazy a joint exercise of Law and Oath would be.</div> </div> </div> </div> When I first read this, I thought it was Law and Order. <br /> <br /> So, I then thought of Invictus proscuters and Carthian cops running a vampire security. It made me smile and laugh.<br /> <br /> Then I realized just how effing scary that would actually be in game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T10:48:39-07:00","id":441600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tchokes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=437350#post437350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmm... not sure I enjoy the Cortoisie Fighting Style.<br /> <br /> There is absolutely no reason why any Invictus wouldn't get it. They are bound to have one of those Abilities at a high level, and for 2 points they can use them in combat when it arises.</div> </div> </div> </div> Reason why Invictus won't get Courtise. <br /> 1) They invested in Dominate, Animalism, Nightmare, and other social disciplines instead of going physical, and see no need of such fighting methods when an eyelock will shut down any combat. <br /> 2) They prefer other weapons. Alternatively, they known Protean.<br /> 3) They specialize in mental or physical skills, and not the social ones to really make it work. Why invest for higher dice pools when its already a high dice pool for you?<br /> 4) A preference for a style of fighting that doesn't involve being a dualist or standing out - Obfuscate stealthy types (nossies and mehket especially) stand out as hating.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One last worry, though... where does this leave the Spina? Are they gone? </div> </div> </div> I don't understand the worry for the Spina. So what if they're not in bloodline form anymore? This is a good thing - it means that the Knights of the Thorned Wreath can include more students than one single lineage. Before, the Knighthood was basically the same thing as the Bloodline. Now, you can have the Knighthood as an entity in every city! And teach the tactics to any student! <br /> <br /> You can mimic the entire old bloodline with some Oaths and Fighting Style. So, now you can be a Gangrel Spina. Or even a Nossie or Ventrue Spina. Or how about a Daeva that's part of that one bloodline that lets them have a host of revenants with them. &quot;How dare you rudely insult my children!&quot; <br /> <br /> I'm personally struck by all the wickedly cool ideas you can do with them now! Mind you, I never was a fan of Covenant Organization = New Bloodline. So, this is better for me. But still, isn't it a good thing overall? You can still play a Spina, but now you can do more with them! <br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=441253#post441253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I think these are terrible. How exactly is Invictus uniquely positioned to prevent the Acolytes from summoning Cthulu and turning the place into Hell on Earth or ensuring kindred society is not overthrown by a Dragon with a god-complex, a few scales and coils, and a couple of ideas on how to make the local kindred more useful to stroking his ego, or even keeping the Sanctified from marching out on a genocidal purge? Acolytes get to construct frankenstein monsters or summon monsters, Dragons get loads of additional psychic powers otherwise closed to vampires and resistances to disciplines, and Carthians (just like Sanctified and Acolyte spellcasters) can mystically deliver unavoidable and unresistable crippling strikes or death blows but the best thing you come up with for Invictus is the ability to skip eating for a few nights if they already have lots of willpower and vitae to blow already.</div> </div> </div> </div> How is that different from 1e? Acolytes and Sanctified did that before, and all Invictus had were social merits. Dragons do have access to unique magic no one else does. Carthian Law was always unavoidable, making even elders powerless before a Carthian In Charge. <br /> <br /> And I'm going to say that you're vastly underestimating Oaths. They're giving me chills.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't care for the oath system because much of it literally rewards oath-breakers and punishes individuals who act in good faith. This is only intensified when you flushed the few restrictions that were the only pretense anyone could claim Oaths are an Invictus signatory ability, as well as the only real deterrence against abuse, down the toilet. </div> </div> </div> Very odd that you think that. I don't see that at all. Handshake rewards the person who forces someone else to fail, but that's not the same as being an oath-breaker yourself. Hard Motherfucker paints a bulls eye on your back if you break it. Breaking Model Prisoner deals you agg damage. <br /> <br /> I don't see it.<br /> <br /> Now, if you mean that some oaths encourage you to backstab your partner? That's a feature, not a bug. Invictus are backstabbers. Its only natural that they are encouraged to do so instead of being honorable all the time. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oath of Abstinence<br /> Because Elders (Invictus and otherwise) don't already have multiple methods of circumventing the vinculum dangers attendant with consuming kindred blood. But don't even think of using your disciplines. </div> </div> </div> Combine with Oath of Fealty. Drawing vitae from that doesn't compromise Oath of Abstinence (I don't think). Full access to your powers. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oath of the Hard Motherfucker<br /> That's a name I expect the Carthians to use in reference to this oath especially due to it's purpose. Why doesn't the Invictus use a name for it that sounds a tad bit more professional and not the ghetto fabulous pejorative currently being used? </div> </div> </div> Welcome to the new Invictus. The Estate is no more all boardrooms than the Ventrue are. They're just as much backroom gangs, bikers, and mobsters. On college, they're the privileged sororities and fraternities. Also, the Estate is very much into backstabbing and viciousness. This Oath is supposed to very much provide a counterpoint to the darker side of the Estate. The whole point is being a departure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oath of the Safe Word<br /> This strikes me as something that would be used as a punitive judgement for a minor offense. </div> </div> </div> Which is why you only use it with someone you trust. And remember that it hurts both individuals who break it. Together, the two are stronger than one. Joint merits, joint willpower. Break it, it hurts someone temporarily, and both lose the benefits. Using it for a punishment when working together is vastly superior? <br /> <br /> You can set it up so that, at some point, you break it and cripple your other side during a critical moment. Which is frankly in style with backstabbing Invictus. But as punishment for a minor offense? That's a very quick way of earning a reputation of being a backstabber whom no one will trust in an oath.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oath of the Handshake Deal<br /> Can covenant status be offered as collateral? Because if so, this is the &quot;I steal ur powrz&quot; power like everyone else has gotten. </div> </div> </div> Assuming you don't want whatever you asked for in the first place. And, remember, stealing something else can come with high social penalties. And, as always, constant backstabbery can earn you a reputation. Got to be conniving and traitorous in moderation. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oath of the Refugee<br /> You have status equal to zero when you flee a city so you cancel out zero successes to any efforts to pursue or attack you. Also, why wouldn't the Sanctity of Merits apply when you lost the attendant city and covenant status? </div> </div> </div> One, you don't necessarily lose the covenant status. In fact, the merit flat out implies you don't - otherwise, how else would you be able to subtract it from being tracked? <br /> <br /> As well, once you give up the Oath, you get an increase of popularity with your new home automatically. Defense against being tracked and free city status so they HAVE to take you in? Plus a rise in the eyes of the Estate? What's there not to like?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oath of the Model Prisoner<br /> This one makes no sense to me. In my experience kindred taken prisoner (and if it's known they are kindred) are kept staked when they aren't being actively questioned or needed conscious for an experiment until or unless they are released. It's easier to hide or transport them when you can stuff them in a duffel bag or throw them in a shallow grave or freezer and not actually worry about killing them permanently. Keeping them in torpor also means (most of the time) the captive can't spend idle time plotting to use Protean, Obfuscate, Dominate, Majesty, Animalism, Nightmare etc. to overpower their captors and flee. Since this oath explicitly doesn't require a notary and does direct Aggravated or Lethal damage it has the greatest potential for abuse. But we'll pretend for a moment that vampires are not pragmatic and that they follow the Geneva Conventions. Creative applications can have this oath apply to being kidnapped or otherwise 'unjustly' detained. Even overthrow a prince. Captors can get around the restrictions by subcontracting interrogation or imprisonment to individuals or groups who are not covenant members. </div> </div> </div> You are right. Sending prisoners into torpor is standard operating procedure. Thus, the Oath. It FORCES captors to treat you nicely, to not shove you into torpor. Its leverage. This is the exception that forces your captors to follow Geneva Conventions instead of doing whatever they want. And, yes, it applies to kidnappers as well. <br /> <br /> None of this is creative. Its pretty much the reason d'etre of it all. Your complaints seem to be the whole point of the merit. <br /> <br /> Actually, that's true of almost all the Oaths. You might just not be someone who'd enjoy playing a member of the new Invictus. Because the backstabbing and manipulation is the point of all this, and you're calling it a flaw or problem. Its all features, not bugs. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oath of the True Knight<br /> Does this oath require you to end previously existing oaths and vinculums and forswear other covenant and city (and possibly clan) affiliations first, or does it dissolve them when the oath is taken. Everyone else so far has gotten the ability to become immune to vinculums or break the blood bond prematurely, so I see no particular reason why it wouldn't dissolve pre-existing obligations. But it's unclear on that point as well as whether or not its the knight or the one attempting to force a vinculum as the one who takes Aggravated damage. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Invested<br /> As has been stated previously, another merit already exists with the same name. This is a cut and paste of the same merit every other covenant has gotten to give PCs a jump on status accumulation into a covenant they don't currently belong to formally.<br /> I don't like these merits because if you have a non-hostile relationship with someone in a given covenant you should already be able to trade minor favors in the form of a single dot of a social merit already. If you're referring to the limited access to their covenant signature abilities like Coils and Cruac, well, Invictus doesn't have any signature abilities to share and they don't have any useful merits requiring more than one covenant status to obtain, so why bother? </div> </div> </div> Then don't allow it at your table? That simple, really. But in cities where the Lance and Estate are buddies? It makes sense that they have influence with each other, show up at Mass and Estate meetings, etc. This merit reflects that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Courtoisie<br /> Considering some of the comments in this thread, it's obvious that it's not being taken seriously as a fighting style. Then again, not only does it use the same name as the bloodline signature discipline of the foppish Spina bloodline, it's a subpar fighting style currently. While the other covenants actually has abilities to improve their survivability or lethal ability in combat, the Invictus opts to becomes Spider-man, trading quips during a fight for actual lethality. The only really useful ability is Establish the Duel and that's only IF it works automatically even if another character is attempting to sneak up on you to stab you in the back using Obfuscate and breaks the discipline's effects. It's not even particularly useful against multiple attackers because switching to the more dangerous foe or not persisting in beating on someone who's fleeing, torpid, or dead, ends the benefit. </div> </div> </div> Oh, its an awesome Fighting Style. Most of the discussion seems to be more around the loss of Courtise as a bloodline discipline than anything. The point is to force a one-on-one fight between you and someone else. Not be better, but to force it to happen. All you need to do is pick someone weak, then kill them off, and others won't touch you as you do this. Well, it'll hurt them to try. And your target can't even run away, so its great as an execution style! Its very tricky, and I love it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Crowdsourcing<br /> This looks like a variant of Carthian Pull and Attache applied to PCs instead of a Retainer. This is sort of something I could see a Commissioner in Invictus having but since they officially don't have any titles beyond Notary, and that was rendered obsolete with the proposal regarding oaths here. Why should anyone bother with more than one dot? Why do you need Academics, it has nothing to do with gaining or applying a formal education? Unless Carthian Pull is hard capped at 5, it's superior to Crowdsourcing. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Moderator<br /> Another one where nobody should actually bother with more than one dot. Someone with 3 ranks in Computers should already be able to use the Internet as a 1 dot Library, Allies, or Contacts with limited value and functionality. </div> </div> </div> That's not true according to the rules. Computer allows hacking, programming, and internet searching as actions. You still have to buy specific Libraries, Contacts, or Allies if you want some in depth information that's more than what you'll find in blogs or published material. <br /> <br /> Especially not on obscure topics like vampire lore or Invictus history from across the ocean, which this does allow. You can remain in contact with Invictus vampires across the world with this, basically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Information Network<br /> Unless the specialty is interdisciplinary or considered an area of expertise, this merit isn't worth purchasing. </div> </div> </div> If you have a lot of Contacts, that's a lot of free specialties, not only across a number of skills, but across for each Contact. For someone with Professional Training, Moderator, or any other way of getting lots of contacts cheaply, this is pretty nice. And, remember, specialties stack. That's potentially a lot of dice for one merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tech Savvy<br /> While there is an actual mechanical purpose to the tiers here, it's unnecessary. You can't jury rig something together that's functional with all those prerequisites already? And since when could you no longer obtain equipment with improved Durability, functionality etc. than the default versions if you had the Resources score? Is this merit supposed to enable Invictus members to obtain equipment type Hunter Endowments? </div> </div> </div> Its free dice for use with a piece of technological equipment. It counts towards high end guns, for instance. <br /> <br /> And, as far as I'm aware, this is the first merit that provides equipment with better durability and functionality as the default versions with Resources. If, you have Resources 3 and Tech Savvy 3, you can get any equipment rated at Availability 5, and it will be superior to anyone else's Availability equipment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Noblesse Oblige<br /> This merit may not be advisable for someone who is upwardly mobile since they would likely lose their official position for another one if they got promoted. But I can also see it as a mechanic who's purpose is to actually kill any desire for upward mobility. </div> </div> </div> Depends on the position. Some positions come with upwards mobility. A harpy position can grow in prestige, after all. A junior Sheriff assistant becoming full Sheriff wouldn't be considered a loss of official position, in my opinion. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Social Engineering<br /> Interesting idea, kind of lackluster in some of the effects for a four dot merit with some extensive prerequisites. There are no examples for using social engineering to prop someone up (in other words, moving a mortal associate up within an organization to where he's a more useful retainer or ally, or even a kindred protege.) </div> </div> </div> A ten minute window of free access to someone's Haven? How is that not HUGE?<br /> <br /> Removing someone's covenant status with dirt you've dug up on them, effectively turning them into a pariah? You can't instantly buy something back with Sanctity of Merits - you kinda do need to justify the new purchase, after all. The idea is that you don't lose experience points for something that can be destroyed, not that your merits can't be destroyed.<br /> <br /> The +1 bonus is designed to be shared with everyone as possible. That means that the entire city is getting an edge at heckling the target. Its blood in the water, causing sharks to circle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T20:25:41-07:00","id":451245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=441253#post441253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I think these are terrible. How exactly is Invictus uniquely positioned to prevent the Acolytes from summoning Cthulu and turning the place into Hell on Earth or ensuring kindred society is not overthrown by a Dragon with a god-complex, a few scales and coils, and a couple of ideas on how to make the local kindred more useful to stroking his ego, or even keeping the Sanctified from marching out on a genocidal purge? Acolytes get to construct frankenstein monsters or summon monsters, Dragons get loads of additional psychic powers otherwise closed to vampires and resistances to disciplines, and Carthians (just like Sanctified and Acolyte spellcasters) can mystically deliver unavoidable and unresistable crippling strikes or death blows but the best thing you come up with for Invictus is the ability to skip eating for a few nights if they already have lots of willpower and vitae to blow already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where the Acolytes have blood sorcery, Where the Sanctified have inquisitors and crusaders, Where the Carthians have overwhelming dice modifiers, the Invictus have numbers. The Acolytes can afford to throw a single powerful thing at something. The sanctified can afford to throw two skilled warriors blessed by theban at something. The carthians can outwit anything with scathing dice. The Invictus though, they can afford to throw twenty moderately skilled bodies at the issue and continue to do so relatively indefinitely. The Invictus strength has always been force of numbers. Individually weak, but strong as a community. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=441253#post441253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oath of the Hard Motherfucker<br /> That's a name I expect the Carthians to use in reference to this oath especially due to it's purpose. Why doesn't the Invictus use a name for it that sounds a tad bit more professional and not the ghetto fabulous pejorative currently being used?</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit I don't entirely get this one. Not just because of the name, but also because of the content of the oath. Awarding an invictus for purposefully going out and antagonizing another covenant seems spurious at best. That's not the Invictus way in my mind. They do kill members of other covenants, but not in the way this describes, not in a messy way. So I don't get this oath, I agree. I don't think it belongs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=441253#post441253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Invested<br /> As has been stated previously, another merit already exists with the same name. This is a cut and paste of the same merit every other covenant has gotten to give PCs a jump on status accumulation into a covenant they don't currently belong to formally.<br /> I don't like these merits because if you have a non-hostile relationship with someone in a given covenant you should already be able to trade minor favors in the form of a single dot of a social merit already. If you're referring to the limited access to their covenant signature abilities like Coils and Cruac, well, Invictus doesn't have any signature abilities to share and they don't have any useful merits requiring more than one covenant status to obtain, so why bother?</div> </div> </div> </div>It gives free resources and influence, there's a single reason right there to take it. <br /> <br /> I for one like these 1 dot merits. They're a way for the covenants to represent their pre-joined phases in a merit without having to represent it in a weird way on a sheet or otherwise. Whether or not people like them, it is thematic. People appear to be missing the point of these merits. The Acolyte version was called Chorister because you were a member of the Chorus, you were a potential recruit for the Acolytes. The invictus have invested to represent a paige. You gain some cursory benefits and get a view into the life. As it should be. Rather than blame the merit and immediately bring up Cruac for instance, you should instead be reminding your players that no self respecting acolyte would be teaching any member of the chorus cruac because no member of the chorus is expected to survive the ordeal - we'll quietly ignore the fact that choristers are technically still considered outsiders, so you've just taught an outsider cruac which is a death sentence for an acolyte. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5423-oukranos","name":"Oukranos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T05:08:40-07:00","id":451437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oukranos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=451245#post451245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit I don't entirely get this one. Not just because of the name, but also because of the content of the oath. Awarding an invictus for purposefully going out and antagonizing another covenant seems spurious at best. That's not the Invictus way in my mind. They do kill members of other covenants, but not in the way this describes, not in a messy way. So I don't get this oath, I agree. I don't think it belongs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider the flavour of this Oath. It is made by Unconquered Neonates. Perhaps even those minted by gang culture, instead of the Feudalism or New Money of Elder Invictus. The point is for the young to prove themselves... by capping the competition. I would imagine many older members of the covenant dislike or outright reject this Oath, but that does not change that the young invented and use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T08:06:19-07:00","id":451529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=451437#post451437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Consider the flavour of this Oath. It is made by Unconquered Neonates. Perhaps even those minted by gang culture, instead of the Feudalism or New Money of Elder Invictus. The point is for the young to prove themselves... by capping the competition. I would imagine many older members of the covenant dislike or outright reject this Oath, but that does not change that the young invented and use it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I could see that. Separation of the old and new, but if that was the goal, I would have liked to see more of it in the oaths. I think that if I use that as my field of view, it's pretty clear in the merits section where that separation is: see tech saavy versus noblesse oblige for instance. However, the oaths don't really seem to have that separation except in this one oath. Would have liked to see more 'new blood' oaths if that was the intention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5423-oukranos","name":"Oukranos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T09:19:42-07:00","id":451606,"title":"","content":"It's obscene schlock to appeal to the lowest common denominator nothing more. If it was a departure from the format of a simple self explanatory title to degrading insults leveled the oath taker then where's the Oath of the Poonhound or Oath of the PMSing Feminazi? If it's a simple acknowledgement that the Invictus embraces pop culture then Oath of the O G Pimp is sufficient and certainly a more realistic application of the slang terms that contemporaries of the late 20th early 21st century would use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T09:55:16-07:00","id":451621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oukranos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=451529#post451529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see that. Separation of the old and new, but if that was the goal, I would have liked to see more of it in the oaths. I think that if I use that as my field of view, it's pretty clear in the merits section where that separation is: see tech saavy versus noblesse oblige for instance. However, the oaths don't really seem to have that separation except in this one oath. Would have liked to see more 'new blood' oaths if that was the intention.</div> </div> </div> </div>To add on to what saibot said.<br /> <br /> Its more than just &quot;new blood.&quot; Its meant to showcase that the Invictus is heavily invested in being criminal organizations, not just boardrooms. The Estate are as much the thugs ruling over the drug trade on the streets as they are the corporate sharks ruling a fortune 500 company, or some old fashioned vamp with ideas of noble obligations. It is crass, hard edged, and mean, because that's the kind of thing that the Estate have in their membership. Its a merit to highlight a specific style of Invictus that's directly tied to gang culture.<br /> <br /> I feel that the main raison d'etre of this merit isn't to showcase the young, but to showcase the Estate being neck-deep in a wide variety of cultures, that their Oath system isn't tied to some neo-Victorianism. Its a shocking divergence (yes, I think it does use shock tactics) from the usual to deliberately provoke readers into thinking about how the Oaths and everything fit into different cultures. I mean, heck. I can see Courtise being used by someone that takes this Oath.<br /> <br /> And, yes, a few more sprinkled around would help. Even if its just rewording a few of them to make them fit that way. <br /> <br /> It is odd that we're specifying Carthians specifically - while I get that the Movement is the usual rival of the Estate, there are times when its the other covenants, and a general Oath should really be flexible. Like, mention that some cities that adopt it target the Lance or Ordo as their rivals, for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T19:05:57-07:00","id":452211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=451606#post451606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's obscene schlock to appeal to the lowest common denominator nothing more. If it was a departure from the format of a simple self explanatory title to degrading insults leveled the oath taker then where's the Oath of the Poonhound or Oath of the PMSing Feminazi? If it's a simple acknowledgement that the Invictus embraces pop culture then Oath of the O G Pimp is sufficient and certainly a more realistic application of the slang terms that contemporaries of the late 20th early 21st century would use.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">This is a bit much. Please remember rules 1 and 2, to respect others and to respect the conversation.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T20:01:54-07:00","id":452227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=451606#post451606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's obscene schlock to appeal to the lowest common denominator nothing more. If it was a departure from the format of a simple self explanatory title to degrading insults leveled the oath taker then where's the Oath of the Poonhound or Oath of the PMSing Feminazi? If it's a simple acknowledgement that the Invictus embraces pop culture then Oath of the O G Pimp is sufficient and certainly a more realistic application of the slang terms that contemporaries of the late 20th early 21st century would use.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Hard Motherfucker&quot; is actually a <i>compliment</i>. Slang-wise, it's a bit archaic (late mid 1900s), but it <i>basically</i> means that <i>this is a person you don't mess with, because then they will kill you just to watch you die.</i> Like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bDktBZzQIiU\" target=\"_blank\">Johnny Cash</a>.<br /> <br /> Something none of the terms you bring up convey.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T06:37:35-07:00","id":452615,"title":"","content":"Man, I don't know where you guys live, but in New York City, I still hear Hard Motherfucker all the time. Maybe people aren't always using it seriously anymore, but that hardly seems like it's dead.<br /> <br /> Remember that song HAM by Kanye from a couple of years ago? Guess what the acronym stands for!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T07:03:38-07:00","id":452621,"title":"","content":"Actually, the one thing I want to talk about, but no one has brought up, is that there seems to be some hurt over the idea that Spina theoretically won't be a bloodline going forwards, due to Courtise now being a Fighting Style (well, a potential one).<br /> <br /> I'd actually like to hear why people are disappointed. I mean, you still can make a character like that with the Fighting Style, the attitude, and be a member of the Thorned Wreath. What about the bloodline was so attractive that people are so vocally sad about it coming back in a way that -more- can partake of its goodness?<br /> <br /> Charlaquin, you voiced some dismay on the matter. Can you give your feelings on the matter? I don't respond negatively, or say how your feelings are wrong, or anything. I actually would really like to know, since the Spina had some popularity with my group, and I want to know before they see this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-22-2015, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T10:26:17-07:00","id":452826,"title":"","content":"I have a feeling at least some of the negative reactions come from the loss of exclusivity. As a Bloodline-specific power, it used to be something that marked your character as special. Not just anybody could learn Courtise, you had to be a decoder-ring-carrying member of the secret Spina club. Now that it's available to any Invictus, it doesn't feel as unique. That doesn't bother me personally, but I imagine it might bother some.<br /> <br /> I think the majority, however, are just worried this might mean their favorite bloodline won't get updated for 2e. People get very attached to their favorite Z-splats, and with so few 2e-compliment bloodlines, seeing the signature ability of your favorite bloodline updated, but no longer attached to that bloodline could cause one to lose hope for that bloodline ever making it into the new edition.<br /> <br /> I meant for my comment to be lighthearted, I'm really just happy I can make characters that get bonuses for being polite again. But I do wonder if this means Spina will be in Secrets of the Covenants as a bloodline, or if they're being re-imagined as a political faction, or if they will be removed from 2e entirely, or if they'll come back eventually with a new bloodline Gift, or what. If anything about seeing Courtise as a general Invictus Fighting Style bothers me, it's just that uncertainty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T11:58:50-07:00","id":452964,"title":"","content":"Has anyone tried these, or the merits from other peeks out in playtesting? My vampire game ended shortly before the teasers were released, which was a shame because I really would have liked to spice up Cruac more. I'm in a new game now but it's Werewolf. There's supposed to be vampires around and theoretically some of the merits might be open to my character to try them out but until then I'm more interested in how people have found them working out in their game, instead of what they feel about the names or differences they imply from first edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T21:06:00-07:00","id":453763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oukranos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=451245#post451245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where the Acolytes have blood sorcery, Where the Sanctified have inquisitors and crusaders, Where the Carthians have overwhelming dice modifiers, the Invictus have numbers. The Acolytes can afford to throw a single powerful thing at something. The sanctified can afford to throw two skilled warriors blessed by theban at something. The carthians can outwit anything with scathing dice. The Invictus though, they can afford to throw twenty moderately skilled bodies at the issue and continue to do so relatively indefinitely. The Invictus strength has always been force of numbers. Individually weak, but strong as a community.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to see this concept mechanized more directly. The Carthians get an ability to &quot;summon&quot; a group of nameless thugs, for example, to intimidate or curb dance a low level rival. That seems more about numbers and backup ready minions / friends. <br /> <br /> I also think there should be more universal mechanics for Oathbreakers, rather than the smaller sub-mechanics woven into the individual oaths. The on-the-ground network of the Estate would be a great counter to the mystical-philosophical Carthian Law, for example. You break an Oath, and you get the Oathbreaker Condition. Cue that condition to things like <i>Hard Motherfucker</i> - you don't have to kill a Carthian, you can kill anyone with the Oathbreaker condition to be brought into the gang. You could even have the condition scale like Tempted and inflict on-the-ground network penalties:<br /> <br /> <b>Condition: Oath Breaker</b><ul><li><i>Mechanics</i>: You just gave the finger to the Estate. Maybe they pushed you too far. Maybe they asked you for something too big. Maybe you just got tired of doing things for that shithead notary and his weasel-words. Whatever the reason you broke the Oath doesn't really matter. What matters is you got caught breaking it and now the Estate is coming down on you like a hammer. If you have any of the following Merits, put a line through your last dot for each of them. You cannot access that dot until this condition is resolved. Merits: Allies, Contacts, Resources, Herd, Invictus Status. This condition stacks if you break multiple Oaths, each instance must be resolved separately.</li> <li><i>Beat</i>: Some Merits (Ex: Oath of the Hard Motherfucker) allow Estate members to target Oathbreakers for payback. Take a beat whenever you get hit with that kind of payback.</li> <li><i>Resolution</i>: Fulfill the equivalent of a major boon to the Invictus member with the highest City Status.</li> </ul>Anything that mechanizes that feeling of a syndicate / network / organization beyond just leaving it to roleplay / drama. You could use the condition for all sorts of payback Merits: <i>Estate Enforcer</i> - get a damage bonus against Oathbreakers. <i>Fool Me Once</i> - Gain an initiative bonus against Oathbreakers, or you can never be surprised in combat by an Oathbreaker. And that's just gang-style combat ideas.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T17:55:46-07:00","id":455065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=452615#post452615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, I don't know where you guys live, but in New York City, I still hear Hard Motherfucker all the time. Maybe people aren't always using it seriously anymore, but that hardly seems like it's dead.<br /> <br /> Remember that song HAM by Kanye from a couple of years ago? Guess what the acronym stands for!</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider the reference caught.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T17:56:52-07:00","id":455067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=452621#post452621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the one thing I want to talk about, but no one has brought up, is that there seems to be some hurt over the idea that Spina theoretically won't be a bloodline going forwards, due to Courtise now being a Fighting Style (well, a potential one).<br /> <br /> I'd actually like to hear why people are disappointed. I mean, you still can make a character like that with the Fighting Style, the attitude, and be a member of the Thorned Wreath. What about the bloodline was so attractive that people are so vocally sad about it coming back in a way that -more- can partake of its goodness?<br /> <br /> Charlaquin, you voiced some dismay on the matter. Can you give your feelings on the matter? I don't respond negatively, or say how your feelings are wrong, or anything. I actually would really like to know, since the Spina had some popularity with my group, and I want to know before they see this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, my intention was to redesign the Spina for the blog, and add some Devotions that complement the Fighting Style in this book. But I think there's a backlog; I've got a couple sent to Rose that she hasn't had the time to get posted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T14:49:04-07:00","id":489882,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Assorted Playtesting observations if these are still useful:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Crowdsourcing (CS)</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>General Feelings</i>: The action has some limited applications. The suppression effect means that unless you're getting something you can't normally get, it will usually be better to go for alternate means of gaining equivalent bonuses (Social Maneuvering, Boon Exchange, etc). Two points where it did seem useful - giving the bump to 6+ dots, and pressing tasks where the coterie / individual is a few points short of solving a problem. Though the latter is slightly hampered by the time cost of the action itself.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>Specific Question</i>: Dots gifted from one Kindred to another are suppressed for the remainder of the story. This does NOT seem to apply to the receiver. So - My character with 5 Dots in Allies acts as the hub. Coterie-mate with 3 Dots in CS gains three successes on the CS roll. Three other Kindred can now gift one dot of allies to me each. After the massive 8-dot Ally maneuver which triggers a state-wide recall election for the governor, the three Kindred who gave me ally dots lose them. But do I? As the text references only the &quot;shifts&quot; disappear, my interpretation was the hub character should not lose them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Information Network (IN)</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>General Feelings</i>: Each contact grants a focused skill specialty relating to the details of the contact in question. The clause we got stuck on was the &quot;applicable only on information gained from the contact.&quot; This caused two effects: Either live conversations with the contact would be drawn out as the player tried to get as much information as possible before walking into a situation, or play would get broken during scenes as the player reached out to the contact as &quot;new&quot; information was needed on the ground. To address that flow, we just made it much more abstract in nature - as long as it was something your contact would reasonably have given you information on, we assumed it happened offscreen. A a slight balance, we didn't let the other specialty-enhancing merits piggyback off these (Interdisciplinary, etc).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Invested (I)</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>General Feelings</i>: We didn't think the 'Merits for Favors' clause would see much traction, since trading merits for favors is pretty much the local Invictus shtick and you didn't need a merit to do it. However, it ended up being more an offscreen hook for the player:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">&quot;I need Contacts: Street to start looking for that runaway.&quot;</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">&quot;These three Invictus characters would be known to have that. Who would you approach and what would you offer?&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Player than made an offer which was reasonable, deal was done. Didn't take much on-screen negotiation, and I think by allowing the player to choose the favor that was done, there was more connection to it. A stepping stone for further relationship between that character/NPC. Unless there was literally no character I could think of with the type of sought Merit, I always tried to make it a non-Generic character re: the favor.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Also, we discovered this Merit works well for someone leaving the Invictus on good terms and keeping connections with old allies / family.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Noblesse Oblige (NO)</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>General Feelings</i>: We immediately ditched the City Status requirement for this so as to open it up to low status positions (Hound, etc) and to Clan (Priscus) and Covenant (Varied/Many). The three dot cost seemed rather steep for basically swapping out one touchstone for another. YMMV, but positions are a little more fluid for us, so you were subjecting yourself to a more vulnerable touchstone, and not actually gaining much of a mechanical advantage. We decided that rather than <i>replacing </i>the Touchstone outright, you would anchor this Merit to an existing Touchstone. You would then gain any benefits from that Touchstone by <b>either </b>interacting with the Touchstone as normal, <b>or </b>by interacting / fulfilling the duties of your office. This led to thematic joining in some fashion, either the anchor Touchstone represented an aspect of the office, or interactions with the touchstone became flavored with themes of the office. And then finally, we ruled that loss of the position just meant you could no longer access the benefits, though we decided that using Sanctity of Merits to get these dots back would be a <b>Humanity 3: Two Dice</b> breaking point as the character admits to themselves that they failed. Alternately, they could leave the dots on the sheet in belief that they would earn / wrest the position back but in the meantime got no benefits.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Social Engineering (SE)</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>General Feelings</i>: Merit is very good. Learning banes and destroying havens are massive advantages against an enemy, let alone an ally. The social bonus / penalty to a single roll is definitely the weakest option, and was only taken when 4+ successes had been rolled by the base rules. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>Specific Questions</i>: There was some discussion on if a single option could be taken more than once with multiple successes. Could you just learn three different banes/conditions on the target, get 30 minutes in the haven, or get (+3) to a social roll on the target? We decided yes, you could stack in that fashion.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>Abuse Issues</i>: The issue almost immediately got abused over the &quot;<i>characters may only be the target of SE once per story.</i>&quot; While we immediately quashed using SE on oneself, a tactical use would be using SE on an ally for no or little effect (-1 to your next intimidate roll!), thus immunizing them from further SE effects from enemies or the like. I quashed that as well, but I feel the rule might be better served with a user-based limitation. Something like: &quot;<i>SE can be used a number of times per story equal to your Invictus Status, and not on the same target more than once.</i>&quot; This would mirror a lot of other X per Story/Session mechanics, while still being extremely valuable, and giving it a bit of buff against the steal/mimic Covenant powers from other groups, while also avoiding the case where Elder Eversecret auto-failed just because Neonate Nosykid got there first. I also gave PCs a beat whenever SE caused them a legit setback.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Oath of the Model Prisoner (OMP)</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>General Feelings</i>: The timing and adjudication of this is too vague. In theory it isn't available to characters without Experience Points. In theory it has to be sworn in the presence of a Notary, etc. More definition is needed on the difference between &quot;intent&quot; and action. We decided that this is an Oath that can be sworn in any domain where a Notary is active and has made a public declaration regarding the oath (specific words of surrender, a specific flavor ritual, etc.) Thereafter anyone who knows the oath details may swear it. If they don't have enough XP on hand, they can suppress skills or merits relating to Combat to balance it out in a pledge of peacefulness. Once the captivity / Oath ends, they get their traits back.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>Specific Questions</i>: </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Trigger timing - when would the damage happen in the following scenario? </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Invictus captured by Carthians.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Invictus prisoner pledges the Oath.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Carthians meet and vote on whether to kill or free the prisoner, one at a time.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Vote is tallied, execution carries.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Carthian captors begin marching to the kindred jail intending the execution.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Carthian captors engage the Invictus Prisoner (initiative) so as to perform the execution.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Carthian captors begin inflicting damage on the Prisoner on each of their combat turns.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Regardless of where the damage starts, would the damage happen every turn one of the above valid moments is hit, or only once per essentially extended action? </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">How do you handle multiple or changing captors thematically? Does the Oath automatically target whoever reasonably has access to the Prisoner, or does the Oath need to be resworn with each new transfer of power? Example - the above Carthians vote for freedom and release the Invictus Prisoner over to the Circle Sheriff. Is the Sheriff now bound by the restrictions of the Oath, or does the Oath have to be re-sworn actively? If it's auto - it becomes more versatile for torpid / staked prisoners. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>Abuse Issues</i>: </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The captors cannot harm the oathbound else they suffer the willpower/health loss - but no mention if they can allow or orchestrate for others to do so. If they can simply look the other way, then effectiveness of the Oath is massively curtailed. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Prince-Slayer Gambit: Invictus Prisoner swears the Oath to Invictus Captors. A gang-squad of every Invictus with Resilience (or who don't mind taking some aggravated damage) attacks the Prisoner. Carthian Prince suffers one lethal per attack. He knows exactly why he's suffering the damage, but does that include where the action is taking place?</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Will have more later.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","user":"Holy","date":". 04-23-2015, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T08:21:29-07:00","id":490585,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Continued Playtesting observations:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Oath of the Refugee (OR)</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>General Feelings</i>: Cool concept, but since most games involve a specific/single Domain, it doesn't see much play with PCs. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>Abuse Issues</i>: The ultimate way to abandon the Invictus. Swear this Oath, leave the Covenant and City (You're gonna lose the Invictus Status anyway) and your old Unconquered friends have just as much trouble finding you as anyone else.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Oath of the Righteous Kill (ORK)</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>General Feelings</i>: Very useful merit, though it does feel like there's a missed opportunity here to let the Sanctified compliment the Estate with this Merit. In any case, there were a few areas that needed clarification:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>Specific Questions</i>: Is it purely the Merit-holder's prerogative to allow the Oath to go off? Meaning, does the action in question actually have to be a threat to the Invictus / Masquerade? Or do you just need to convince the Merit-holder it is? (via Social Maneuvering, Disciplines, etc.)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What exactly does the clause '<i>She checks for Detachment as if she committed the crime herself</i>' intend? Does that mean that the breaking point mystically transfers to the Merit-holder at (+1) die, regardless of the Merit-holder's current Humanity or Banes? Or does the Merit Holder get to ignore any breaking points entirely if they wouldn't normally be an issue, either being above her Humanity rating or because she's taken a bane for that sin? We did the latter, making low-humanity bane-riddled confessors the best confessors - though that did feel a little clashing with the theme of encouraging sympathy / empathy. Felt better to have the Elder talk about duty, service and the meaninglessness of human weakness, let alone humans themselves, in the protection of the Masquerade. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Unclear on how specific or broad the &quot;action&quot; has to be. Might be a good place for a narrative example to give some guidance, especially concerning if multiple sins are committed in the action. Let's say that to defend the Masquerade, a mid-level Invictus is sent to kidnap a mortal, determine if the mortal has told anyone else, then track down anyone they may have told, in each case either erasing memories or killing the mortal in question. Do the two Oathbound need to make a laundry list of possible sins? (Impassioned violence, removing consent with a discipline, premeditated murder, to name the obvious.) Or should the Oath auto-trigger on the next instance of a sin in pursuit of the action, and then need to be resworn?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Oath of the Safe Word (OSW)</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>General Feelings</i>: Cool thematic idea, but practically the risks are too big. At the end of the day, you're paying 2xp on an Oath which gives you in the best case a 5xp Social Merit. So - a 3xp freebie. Then there is the Willpower exchange. This is very tricky thing to adjudicate between a PC/NPC as the Storyteller. How much Willpower does a reasonable NPC allow to be taken per story? How many should the NPC take in return? Does the loss of willpower actually register in a sensory way for either party? I may know when I'm low on Willpower, but will the other Oathbound? And then there is the death-knell risk. If the paralyzation clause were only available to the to Oathbound, it's already steep. But open the door to the fact that one of the two could be forced/leveraged by others to trigger the paralyzation, and you not only need to keep the other person happy, you need to keep it all a secret.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>Abuse Issues</i>: Why would an Elder not hedge her bets with a Neonate by using entombed command (Do not break this oath without warning me first.) Or using any other number of ways to assuage an inferior kindred? As above, very risky. And if the neonate / inferior doesn't plan on utilizing the kill-buff as part of the process, other Oaths are more effective at both the benefits and the consequences. Oath of Fealty for a simple one. Oath of Action is very popular - get access to a (potentially) 5-dot discipline, perform a trivial service or let a month pass, and inflict some damage on the Elder as some final payback.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Oath of the True Knight (OTK)</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>General Feelings</i>: This is the scary one. An armor bonus, immunity to Vinculums, and discipline defense. All good stuff. Some clarifications:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>Specific Questions</i>: The Oathtaker cannot be subject to Vinculum or other individual Oaths. First - does that mean a full 3-step Vinculum, or any step at all (which brings to mind more the Oath of the <i>Virginal</i> Knight, if the Oathbound cannot have ingested any blood previously).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Second - Ingested Kindred blood turns to ash in the True Knight's mouth. How does a Knight who can only consume Kindred vitae survive this? I would normally think by Oaths of Fealty or Penance so they can get in on the mystical transfers of vitae - but those require swearing an Oath to an individual, which seems to be prohibited as well for the True Knight. Oath of Abstinence doesn't seem like a viable choice either for a combat-focused role. Or - does the Knight only need to be free of individual Oaths at the time of the swearing, but after becoming a True Knight can swear individual Oaths as needed?<br /> <br /> Alright, I hope any of this helps. I love the Invictus and am excited to see all this come out. Thanks again for the open dev opportunities.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T19:48:49-07:00","id":513650,"title":"","content":"I was under the assumption that if you are Invictus, somewhere along the line you get some oath or power that allows you to be a better lord of a domain than the next guy. I have read all the oaths and merits here and people's responses. I could not find a good ability/power that allows you to control things. Most of these powers seem excellent things for the low-mid tier kindred and helps them to be better organizers and contribute to the society they are in over all, which is great, as low level invictus was really in need of some love.<br /> But I think the Invictus elders need something that is actually useful to control domains, similar to the discipline Tenure in Invictus covenant book. Without the ability to control and limit what is going on in their domains, Invictus is less of a good choice for elders and actual domain lords than almost any other covenant. Oaths that prevent people from doing things you dont want are extremely weak in my opinion except for dealing damage which can easily be healed since the oath breaker can easily prepare for this beforehand (ie. break the oath at a time of his choosing). There is also the added benefit of realizing someone broke the oath and that is as good as it gets.<br /> My interpretation is that this 'new invictus' mentality is join up when you are new, reap whatever benefits you can get(which is not all that great, but a stepping stone if no other covenant has you), then eventually join up with another covenant including carthians which grants you more powerful abilities and actually the ability to control your domain properly.<br /> One argument posted above was that the invictus has numbers, and thats its advantage. It is really hard to imagine in reality what is actually granting these numbers. I find it hard to believe it is the multitudes of free or easy to access social merits that allow invictus to hold such great numbers. I would assume if i get 10 players at a table, invictus would have trouble to get the majority of members if the actual benefits of the covenant was presented.<br /> As it currently stands the dragon with the voivode coil and the more-powerful-than-god-machine carthian law is easily out performing the powers invictus has at its disposal to control a domain. I would assume a prince or domain lord would rarely need additional merits, or oaths that can be broken left and right with no real penalties, the other covenants simply make better domain lords and princes. I dont know how much crunch the fluff can handle. But it looks less than convincing to me that an actual powerhouse would bother with tons of oaths and dozens of merits when other options are irresistable, unstoppable and simply more powerful.<br /> I think these powers are very cool, if some of them require a bit extra attention (game time wise) to get full benefits out of, and I actually think a covenants powers should be similar to this. I just think without a way to counter the carthian law it is pointless to invest into them. I would assume it would require a similar effort to manage votes for a powerful law to pass, as it is to manage tons of oaths to hold a domain. And law is unbreakable.<br /> In spirit of open development (and a bit humor) and to give a suggestion let me give a simple example, this follows the same swearing oath by oneself logic:<br /> <br /> I Am the Hard Motherfucker (Oath of Sovereignty)<br /> Prerequisite: Invictus Status 4, Blood Potency 5 etc. etc.<br /> <br /> This is an oath sworn by oneself. Once you swear it you are a hard motherfucker. Combine all your vassal's city status. The total is deducted form any carthian law status accumulation attempts on you (reduce the total carthian status collected by the lynch mob). If you gather enough status points more than the total carthian status bearing cathians in the city, the law no longer applies to you. You can grant this immunity to others if they swear an oath of service to you. If you have vassals who have vassals, count them as well. Ie. a prince gets the regent's as well as regent's vassals and tenants for his total.<br /> For any other blanket city leveling power, count all your vassals relevant power stats. Apply the same procedure. If the theoretical power uses primal-urge of 8 werewolves, then count your vassal's blood potency to counter it. This only applies to blanket city crippling powers (ie. werewolf trying to flood the whole city, archmage trying to incinerate your city etc. if you have such cosmic stuff in your campaigns, if you like archmages incinerating cities, dont use this last part, hopefully it shouldn't be necessary anyways).<br /> <br /> I am just leaving this here, in case anyone finds interesting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4110-necromter","name":"Necromter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T23:27:30-07:00","id":542327,"title":"","content":"About the Oath of Handshake Deal. How many dots in Merit are used in the <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">collateral?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T05:49:43-07:00","id":542476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=542327#post542327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the Oath of Handshake Deal. How many dots in Merit are used in the <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">collateral?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> I would imagine it depends on the wording of the deal that the vampires strike. &quot;I'll introduce you to my contacts in the police&quot; would probably be the entire Allies (Police) 3, but &quot;I'll introduce you to some of my contacts in the police&quot; would only yield one dot. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T23:55:57-08:00","id":828041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=455067#post455067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, my intention was to redesign the Spina for the blog, and add some Devotions that complement the Fighting Style in this book. But I think there's a backlog; I've got a couple sent to Rose that she hasn't had the time to get posted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh where for art thou, Bloodline blogs. You are missed!<br /> <br /> Sidenote: Could we get anything related to this mysterious InBoard spoiled? A hint maybe? I'd love some idea of how to contextualize its benefits, especially vis-a-vis the Moderator merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T02:04:00-08:00","id":828083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=828041#post828041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh where for art thou, Bloodline blogs. You are missed!<br /> <br /> Sidenote: Could we get anything related to this mysterious InBoard spoiled? A hint maybe? I'd love some idea of how to contextualize its benefits, especially vis-a-vis the Moderator merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno! I gave Rose one full bloodline, and a couple of pitches for others. I'd love to do more. <br /> <br /> And InBoard should be mentioned a bit in the Invictus chapter of the book; I think it was a relatively important element in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T17:28:03-08:00","id":828516,"title":"","content":"Much obliged. Out of curiousity, did any of these merits get tweaked further before going into Secrets of the Covenant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T19:33:25-08:00","id":828555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=828516#post828516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Much obliged. Out of curiousity, did any of these merits get tweaked further before going into Secrets of the Covenant?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't remember, honestly. I did do revisions for them, per Rose's redlines. But it's been a while, and I can't find the draft off-hand so I can't answer to what changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T19:34:27-08:00","id":828557,"title":"","content":"Ah well. If you find it and Rose is cool with it, it'd be lovely to hear. I wouldn't mind doing some playtesting of the updated versions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T11:05:55-08:00","id":828872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/430490-invictus-merits-and-oaths-the-ties-that-bind-secrets-of-the-covenants-dev-blog?p=451437#post451437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consider the flavour of this Oath. It is made by Unconquered Neonates. Perhaps even those minted by gang culture, instead of the Feudalism or New Money of Elder Invictus. The point is for the young to prove themselves... by capping the competition. I would imagine many older members of the covenant dislike or outright reject this Oath, but that does not change that the young invented and use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that <i>would </i>be an interesting conflict; &quot;Heretical&quot; Oaths?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T11:21:20-08:00","id":828880,"title":"","content":"Quick question about the Oath of Abstinence.<br /> <br /> Could a Ghoul swear this to her Regnant before the Regnant goes into Torpor, thus allowing the Ghoul to survive until the Regnant wakes up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T15:48:53-08:00","id":829444,"title":"","content":"The Oath of Abstinence only eliminates the vitae expenditure to rise cost (Ghouls don't spend vitae to get up every night.) and they technically don't meet the criteria to pay the activation cost. (No Blood Potency to determine willpower cost.) But assuming you 1. Find a notary willing to cast it on a non vampire (unlikely) and 2. The effect counts for the purposes of not needing to consume vitae every month to renew their ghoul condition and 3. They don't have to spend willpower to activate the oath, they will still lose access to their disciplines and become human once they use up their remaining 2-3 vitae activating powers in the course of their existence without an active regnant. (Half their vitae pool goes down the drain when activating the oath.)<br /> <br /> I don't see the point of it really, if lengthy torpor durations are actually relevant to the story, the ghoul could simply be part of a ghoul family where they still age slower and can use vampire disciplines even when there's no vitae in their system anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 02-13-2016, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}